 Step 1 — Create GitHub token

GitHub:

Profile picture → Settings → Developer settings → Personal access tokens → Tokens (classic) → Generate new token

Step 2 — Add token to Jenkins
Jenkins → Manage Jenkins → Credentials → System → Global credentials → Add Credentials
 
Kind: Username with password
Username: YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME
Password: YOUR_GITHUB_TOKEN
ID: github-private

 Step 3 — Use private repository
Use normal HTTPS repository URL:

https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/YOUR_PRIVATE_REPO.git

Jenkins Pipeline:

pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {
        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                git(
                    branch: 'main',
                    credentialsId: 'github-private',
                    url: 'https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/YOUR_PRIVATE_REPO.git'
                )
            }
        }

        stage('Test') {
            steps {
                sh 'ls -la'
            }
        }
    }
}

#build
